==Battleground==
*900 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 12~20 seconds<sup>360f~600f</sup>.
*40 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.67~4 seconds<sup>20f~120f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*30 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
*20 [[H. Nah]]s spawn after 62 seconds<sup>1,860f</sup>, delay 23.33~33.33 seconds<sup>700f~1,000f</sup>.
*8 [[H. Nah]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Get ready for a very long and very annoying fight. Your best friends for this stage will be either spammable Area Attackers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg]] or [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]], Wave Units like Talented [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza]] or [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] and Long Distance units like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]]. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] can help a lot as she can sync the H. Nahs and reduce their pushing power. You can also use the cat cannon to sync up the H. Nahs. For the Metal Doges, any consistent Critter such as [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] should be able to deal with them easily.

